--TEST--
a class declared in lower case is a hard compiler error, checked on the leading character only — `rule:core-api/casing-checks-the-leading-character`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class thing {
    public static function go(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}
echo thing::go(), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0110]: `thing` must be PascalCase, e.g. `Thing`
  --> case.nvs:2:7
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
